From c95dcd3aee901b503751c02918a687c83b227511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:01:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] custody v2: genesis survives a failed or ambiguous submission
 and a restart

A founder whose createCommittee failed after its share was durable could never
finish: the daemon exited, and on restart it saw a share on disk, skipped
genesis and served a committee the chain did not have (no_committee forever).
A retry in the same process made a new secret and a new committee.

The founder now seals a genesis INTENT (the exact createCommittee arguments:
salt, machine record, Y, code set, identity and host signatures) together with
its share before the first submission. Until the agreed chain shows that
committee at epoch 1 with this machine and key, every retry - a later genesis
call, or the engine's tick after a restart - reads the committee at an agreed
block and:
- confirms it, without re-sending, when the chain already holds it;
- re-sends the SAME transaction (after the same admission check) when the chain
  agrees it is absent;
- reports a conflict, re-sending nothing, when the id holds another machine or
  key.
An unreadable chain throws: absence is never inferred from an error. No retry
ever makes a new secret or committee. The daemon logs an ambiguous genesis and
lets the engine reconcile it instead of exiting.

State without an intent (written by earlier images, such as the live
committee's) is served exactly as before. A share for a committee the chain
does not have and no intent for it (a legacy orphan, whose salt and signature
were never kept) is reported with an explicit LEGACY ORPHAN reason, kept, and
never re-created or deleted (docs/security/secret-custody-v2.md 4.1).

Tests:
- test/custody-v2-genesis-intent.test.mjs: the real member and writer, a vault
  model with the contract's committee id; save failure, lost receipt, failure
  before the chain, in-process retry, unreadable chain (including no release),
  id conflict, legacy committee and orphan.
- custody-v2-e2e: the same faults against the original vault, each with a
  restart from the disk, including an unreachable RPC through the real quorum
  reader.
